# Core (`packages/core`)

## What lives here

- AST nodes and evaluation logic used by parsers, engines, and the CLI.
- Large “tree” subsystem under `packages/core/src/tree/**` (selectors, rulesets, eval, printing, etc.).

## Hotspots

- Extend algorithm: `packages/core/src/tree/util/extend.ts`
- Tree subsystem: `packages/core/src/tree/**`

## Render mode: nested is the DEFAULT

Jess's default render mode is **NESTED** output (`collapseNesting:false`) — a
first-class feature, not an edge case. Serialization/render must honor nested
output; the flat all-less/extend corpus is a testing convenience, not the spec.
Never dismiss nested-mode correctness as "moot" or "deferred". See
`.cursor/rules/subtrees/core__extend.mdc`.

## Architecture priority

- Follow `AGENTS.md` for repo-wide goals.
- For hot-path perf, the canonical checklist is `docs/perf/V8-ARCHITECTURE.md`
  (each numbered invariant, 1-11 at time of writing, + the regression-fixture
  catalogue); enforcement design is
  `docs/architecture/llm-quality-enforcement-design.md`. Load the `perf-architecture`
  skill before editing eval/render/extend, and use the
  `perf-architecture-reviewer` (evidence per invariant) before landing.
- For anything that changes emitted CSS, the canonical checklist is
  `docs/architecture/SEMANTIC-INVARIANTS.md` (8 invariants + incident
  catalogue); the owner decision ledger is
  `docs/architecture/core/DESIGN-DECISIONS.md`. Cite the SETTLED row a
  change relies on or add an OPEN row, and use the `semantics-reviewer`
  (evidence per invariant) before landing. "Matches less.js" is not a
  justification (ledger E1/E2/E5).
- If the work touches the evaluation-model refactor, use
  `docs/architecture/core/HANDOFF.md` as the active queue and
  `docs/architecture/core/AGGRESSIVE-CUTTING-REVIEW.md` before closing a
  queue pass.
- Use `docs/perf/V8-ARCHITECTURE.md` for parked
  performance protocol and reactivation thresholds.
- Do not preserve clone-heavy or materialization-heavy internals just to keep a local slice green if that fights the target runtime model.

## Cross-package testing nuance

Downstream packages (notably `packages/jess`) often resolve `@jesscss/core` via built `lib/` outputs. If core changes, build it before running downstream tests:

- `pnpm --filter @jesscss/core build`
